     "page": 1,
     "text": "Monroe-Anderson Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Kathy Douglas in consultation on September 14, 2025. I appreciate your referral and the detailed medical history you provided.\n\n**Anemia / blood disorders**:\nKathy has a history of anemia due to venous thromboembolism (VTE) secondary to factor V Leiden mutation. Her condition is currently well-controlled without the need for any medications. The most recent lab results confirm stable hemoglobin levels, and there are no signs of acute thromboembolic events.\n\n**Atrial fibrillation (AFib)**:\nKathy has been diagnosed with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation since September 2024. An echocardiogram performed recently has shown no structural abnormalities, and her CHA2DS2-VASc score is 1. She underwent catheter ablation 0.6 years ago and has been asymptomatic since then, with her condition remaining controlled. She is currently taking diltiazem 180 mg daily, which has been effective in managing her heart rhythm.\n\n**Contraception**:\nKathy has been using norethindrone-ethinyl estradiol 1/20 as an oral contraceptive and has a levonorgestrel intrauterine device (IUD) with 52 mg of hormone. Both methods are effective, and she has no reported side effects or complications. \n\n**Rosacea**:\nKathy has rosacea, which has been well-controlled with the use of metronidazole topical 1% cream. She reports minimal facial redness and no active flare-ups.\n\n**Examination and other findings**:\nDuring the examination, Kathy's blood pressure was 139/89 mmHg, and her weight was 138 pounds, which are within normal limits. She reported no chest pain, palpitations, or other concerning symptoms. Her cardiovascular examination was unremarkable, and there were no signs of fluid overload or edema.\n\n**Social history**:\nKathy reports consuming approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations**:\nKathy's anemia, atrial fibrillation, contraception, and rosacea are all currently well-controlled with appropriate management. Her cardiovascular health is stable, and her contraceptive and rosacea management plans are effective. I recommend continuing the current treatment regimens and monitoring for any new symptoms or complications.\n\nThank you for your collaboration and for considering the information provided. Please feel free to reach out if further information is needed or if there are any additional concerns.\n\nBest regards,\n\nDr. Lauren Jones \nFamily Medicine Specialist \nMonroe-Anderson Medical Group\n"
    }
